<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's net reserves down $11 mln by Jan 10.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's net reserves down $11 mln by Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Monday its net international reserves stood at $1.844 billion on January 10, down $11 million from the week before.</p>
<p>In December 1996, international reserves grew $180 million.</p>
<p>The Central Bank gave no reason for the fall in reserves.</p>
<p>Reserves stood at $1.832 billion at the end of last year, up $276 million from the end of 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
